Support systemd-resolved as a DNS forwarder.  The usage of systemd-resolved
is officially supported since SLE 15 SP6, but netconfig was missing an
official integration.

Supporting systemd-resolved allows the user to configure DNS over TLS
without dropping netconfig.  A configuration example is provided in
[netconfig(8)](man:netconfig(8)).

When opting into using systemd-resolved, netconfig is used to configure DNS
servers and DNS search domains on a per-interface basis.  Only interfaces
managed by netconfig will be configured and the loopback interface will
never be configured.

Like our other modules the new systemd DNS module supports the usual
dynamic and static configuration as well as the standard and custom
netconfig DNS policies.  The policy "NetworkManager" will be ignored, as
NetworkManager integrates with systemd-resolved by itself.  When
NetworkManager is used as the network service, the module will not be run
and exit successfully.

When changes to /etc/resolv.conf are made, systemd-resolved will be
reloaded and re-read its configuration files.  On older systems a restart
is required, as reloading the configuration files is only supported since
[systemd v256](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/commit/d30d0b04aed25db711cff8d3b035acc39dba4b57).
